WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
Where does rain go after it lands on your street?

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:09.420
It runs downhill. A paper landscape lets your child watch where it flows and

3
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.420
collects.

4
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:14.773
It takes about twenty-five minutes.

5
00:00:16.013 --> 00:00:19.913
Your child practices guessing where water will go and checking the guess.

6
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:25.273
If you have a watershed map, you can also trace where rain from home drains.

7
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:32.203
Gather white printer paper, washable markers, paper towels, and a shallow metal tray

8
00:00:32.203 --> 00:00:38.343
or plastic tub. Use plain water in a new spray bottle or one that has only held

9
00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:42.263
water. If you use a hole punch, handle it yourself.

10
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.020
Stay beside your child.

11
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.400
Spray only at the paper, away from faces and pets.

12
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.740
Keep paper dots and small marker caps away from children under four.

13
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.520
Count the dots out and back in.

14
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.880
If a child is choking, call nine one one.

15
00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.993
Keep all supplies out of mouths.

16
00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:08.633
Cocoa is toxic to dogs and cats, so keep pets away.

17
00:01:10.013 --> 00:01:11.793
Wipe up cocoa and drips right away.

18
00:01:13.053 --> 00:01:15.893
Put cocoa-covered paper in a bin pets cannot open.

19
00:01:17.173 --> 00:01:20.013
Wash everyone's hands with soap and water when you finish.

20
00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.153
Crumple the paper into a tight ball.

21
00:01:24.493 --> 00:01:26.533
Open it gently, but don't flatten it.

22
00:01:27.593 --> 00:01:28.853
You want hills and valleys.

23
00:01:30.313 --> 00:01:32.293
Ask your child, 'Where is the highest ground?'

24
00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:34.473
Then trace each ridge in brown.

25
00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:38.427
Color one low corner blue and call it the bay.

26
00:01:39.787 --> 00:01:43.307
Tuck a folded towel under the other end, so the bay sits lowest.

27
00:01:44.647 --> 00:01:49.107
Then draw houses, a farm, and a road, some on hilltops and some in valleys.

28
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:54.680
Now point to three spots, one on each side of a ridge and one by a house.

29
00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.080
Ask, 'If rain lands here, where will it go?'

30
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.960
Your child draws a small arrow for each guess.

31
00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.973
Here is a question for you.

32
00:02:04.933 --> 00:02:09.653
Take two drops that land very close together, but on opposite sides of one ridge.

33
00:02:10.893 --> 00:02:12.413
Will they end up in the same place?

34
00:02:17.967 --> 00:02:21.587
Mist the paper from about a foot above, ten to twenty squirts.

35
00:02:22.807 --> 00:02:25.387
It can take several squirts before anything moves.

36
00:02:26.587 --> 00:02:29.207
Then the marker bleeds and runs down the creases.

37
00:02:30.727 --> 00:02:32.787
Drops on each side of a ridge go different ways.

38
00:02:33.867 --> 00:02:35.347
Check the arrows together.

39
00:02:36.787 --> 00:02:38.327
Ask, 'Did the rain go where you guessed?'

40
00:02:38.807 --> 00:02:44.467
Then name it. All the land that drains to the same river or bay is one watershed.

41
00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:48.007
The ridges split one watershed from the next.

42
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.840
A pinch of cocoa near the farm can stand in for fertilizer.

43
00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:59.440
If allergies or asthma rule out cocoa, use colored water with ingredients suitable

44
00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.560
for your child. You can skip both.

45
00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.980
Put a few paper dots on the road as litter.

46
00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.320
Spray again and watch where everything goes.

47
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:15.510
If you have a map of Virginia's watersheds, find your town and follow the river to

48
00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:20.690
where it ends. Have your child pick three things your family can do and draw them.

49
00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.290
They could put trash in the bin or turn off the tap.

50
00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:29.413
Back on your street, rain can carry litter downhill into a storm drain.

51
00:03:30.813 --> 00:03:34.413
Your pan shows how water can pick things up and carry them downstream.
